WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.320
April 2020. Lockdowns
spread across America.

2
00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:07.630
Stores closed. Restaurants sat empty.

3
00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:12.520
In a single month, consumer
spending fell 13.6 percent.

4
00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:16.650
And Americans saved 33 percent
of their disposable income,

5
00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:19.800
up from 12.7 percent in March.

6
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:22.370
Economists say that in any economy,

7
00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:27.640
total spending, total income and
total output must always be equal.

8
00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:32.380
Why? In this mission, you'll map
the economy as a circular flow,

9
00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:35.040
with a product market and a factor market.

10
00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:38.210
Then you'll measure GDP
by adding up spending,

11
00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:40.520
and again by adding up income.

12
00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:44.590
Your mission: find out why
the three totals must match.
